name: Installed Semgrep deadline failure recovers through an approved finite study
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN SEMGREP_AGENT_TOKEN
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed @TMP_HOME
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 Build project context: | prepared-context
submit: use threat-model
submit: options threat-model:import
submit: set path .kuzushi/manual-context.json
submit: set activate false
submit: set label Owned local policy context
submit: run threat-model:import
require-live-snap: 35 threat-model:import saved | imported-context
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | map-result
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-map
paste-file: @ART/deadline-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failure
submit: workbench
nav-mode:
require-live-snap: 25 RESULT failed | deadline-failed
expect-not: u Accept result
ask: Does the real scanner deadline remain a failed Scan with no findings, no automatic acceptance and an inspectable cause?
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-1-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-2-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-3-40x12
ask: Can the operator read deadline recovery at every size without the failed attempt becoming completed work?
resize: 120x36
require-live-snap: 15 RESULT failed | failure-reading-complete
submit: use sast
submit: options sast:scan
submit: set taskMode manual
live-snap: manual-task-mode
submit: set tasks semgrep
live-snap: selected-task-options
paste-file: @ART/rule-setting.txt
keys: Enter
submit: set semgrepTimeoutMs 60000
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study-form
keys: Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CHOOSE DISCOVERY ENGINES | engine-choice
expect: [x] semgrep
keys: a
require-live-snap: 25 Discovery engines  semgrep | selected-engine
keys: L
require-live-snap: 35 Draft ready | fixed-plan
keys: Down Down Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Total calls | total-calls
type: 1
keys: Enter Down Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Protected review | review-calls
type: 1
keys: Enter
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART draft
keys: L End
require-live-snap: 25 y approve | allowance-review
expect: Execution model: none
expect: 60000 ms per job
expect: authentication is separate.
expect: Protected review calls: 1
ask: Does approval disclose three fixed native jobs, one worker and the frozen per-job Semgrep time allowance, with source authentication and model consumption kept honest?
keys: y
require-live-snap: 30 APPROVED STUDY | approved-study
keys: L
require-live-snap: 25 L starts its fixed jobs | fixed-jobs
keys: L
require-live-snap: 30 dispatcher pid | started
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART completed
keys: r
require-live-snap: 30 completed 3 / planned 3 | completed-study
submit: workbench
require-live-snap: 30 Viewing Scan | scan-result
nav-mode:
keys: n
require-live-snap: 25 Viewing Review | accepted-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned policy marker needs an owner decision | policy-finding
expect: signal-only
submit: decision deferred Owned policy marker needs an owner decision
require-live-snap: 25 Owned policy marker needs an owner decision | deferred
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | report
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 15 REPORT | report-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 15 REPORT | report-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 15 REPORT | report-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 15 REPORT | report-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 15 REPORT | report-40x12
keys: NPage NPage NPage
live-snap: report-page-40x12
ask: Are recurrence, the owner decision and coverage limitations readable without turning a harmless policy rule into a vulnerability or fix verdict?
resize: 120x36
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json (4/6) | json-format
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/resume-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 completed 3 / planned 3 | restored-study
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned policy marker needs an owner decision | restored-decision
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/bounded_semgrep.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart preserve the failed deadline attempt, the approved time allowance, three observations and the owner decision without starting more work?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
